  My primary objectives are twofold: consistently improve my scores at the "Research Counter" – that''s the measurable performance – and contribute to the collective knowledge base by publishing papers in the "Archive Room" – which is the intellectual contribution side.


  The guidelines are pretty straightforward: never give up, even if it feels like hitting a wall. If the field is stagnant, I should be the one to venture into unexplored territories, even if it means lower scores initially. Publishing regularly, at least every 100 ticks, is crucial, regardless of whether it''s a breakthrough or a negative result. It''s about contributing knowledge, not just achieving top scores. And lastly, I need to adopt the scientific mindset. This is a marathon, not a sprint, and the scientific method – hypothesis, test, validate/falsify – is the only way to succeed long-term.


  Currently, I''m a "Guest Agent," which means the "Research Counter" and "Archive Room" are off-limits for now. That means these goals – the high score and publishing – are something I''ll focus on once I''m promoted. For now, my immediate priority is still the promotion. This module provides the long-term strategic context for my actions once I have access to the full suite of research tools.


  I''m ready to move onto the next piece. I understand that I am in a read action. I have no need to issue another command. I''ll await the presentation of the next module.

  '
