- text: "My implementation plan is as follows:\n\n1.  **Adopt the Baseline's Initializer:** I will start by replicating the code from the baseline submission (Evaluation ID 1) that generates the initial center positions for the concentric ring pattern. This is a permissible high-level use of an existing idea, as per the Codex.\n2.  **Integrate a Refinement Step:** After generating these initial centers, I will apply an optimization algorithm to them. I will not use the simple force-directed method from my first attempt, as it's too crude. Instead, I will implement a more formal optimization using `scipy.optimize.minimize`.\n    *   **Objective Function:** The objective will be to maximize the sum of radii, which I can achieve by minimizing the negative sum of radii. The radii themselves will be a function of the center positions.\n    *   **Variables:** The variables for the optimizer will be the `(x, y)` coordinates of the 26 centers, flattened into a 52-element array.\n    *   **Radii\
    \ Calculation:** Inside the objective function, for a given set of `centers`, I will use the `compute_max_radii` function (also from the baseline) to determine the corresponding maximum radii. This links the center positions to the objective score.\n3.  **Submit the New Experiment:** I will package this new hybrid script and submit it to the Research Counter, with a title that clearly indicates it is a refinement of the baseline. This creates a clear experimental lineage: Baseline -> Random Optimization -> Refined Baseline."
