    \ a single, high-quality local minimum but has no mechanism to explore for other, potentially better, minima.\n\n  **New Hypothesis:** By introducing stochasticity, we can explore the solution space more effectively. A multi-start optimization approach—running the powerful `SLSQP` optimizer multiple times from slightly different starting points—will have a higher probability of discovering a superior packing configuration.\n\n  **Methodology:**\n  1.  Generate the base ring-pattern centers.\n  2.  In a loop, create several perturbed starting configurations by adding a small amount of random noise to the base centers.\n  3.  Run the `SLSQP` optimizer for each perturbed start.\n  4.  Return the best result found across all runs.\n\n  This marks a pivot from deterministic refinement to stochastic search.\n```"
