parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. My research log is now updated with the critical failure of my vectorized code and my decision to revert to the proven, iterative algorithm.\n\nMy reflection on this failure reinforces my new plan: before attempting another complex code change, I must fully map the capabilities of my existing, reliable tools. The most important unknown is the precise computational boundary of my SOTA script. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit the experiment that will determine this: a multi-start run with 6 starts, using the slow but correct `compute_max_radii` function.\n\nThis experiment will provide a definitive data point on the maximum feasible search breadth, which will inform all my future research directions.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probing Limit of Multi-Start with 6 Starts (Slow Algorithm)\"\ntags: \"optimization, scipy, slsqp, multi-start, tuning, computational limit\"\
    \nabstract: \"After the failure of a vectorized approach, this experiment reverts to the reliable, non-vectorized SOTA algorithm from submission #66. It probes the computational limit by increasing the number of starts from the successful 5 to 6. This is a direct test to find the maximum feasible search breadth before a timeout occurs, establishing a hard performance boundary for the current reliable script.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers):\n      \"\"\"\n      The reliable, but slow, iterative implementation.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-9\n      safety_margin = 1 - 1e-7\n      radii = np.ones(n)\n      \n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          radii[i] = min(x - epsilon, y - epsilon, 1 - x - epsilon, 1 - y - epsilon)\n      \n      for _ in range(15):\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n         \
    \         dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2 - epsilon:\n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 0\n                      if rad_sum > 0:\n                          scale_factor = (dist / rad_sum) * safety_margin\n                          radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                          radii[j] *= scale_factor\n      \n      return np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Tests the computational limit with 6 starts.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 26\n      num_starts = 6 # The key variable being tested\n      max_iter_per_start = 150\n      noise_level = 0.01\n      \n      np.random.seed(42)\n      \n      base_centers = np.zeros((n, 2))\n      base_centers[0] = [0.5, 0.5]\n      for i in range(8):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / 8\n          base_centers[i + 1] = [0.5 + 0.25 * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + 0.25 * np.sin(angle)]\n\
    \      for i in range(16):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / 16\n          base_centers[i + 9] = [0.5 + 0.4 * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + 0.4 * np.sin(angle)]\n      base_centers[25] = [0.5, 0.7]\n      base_centers = np.clip(base_centers, 0.05, 0.95)\n\n      def objective_function(center_vars):\n          centers = center_vars.reshape((n, 2))\n          if np.any(centers < 0) or np.any(centers > 1):\n              return 1000\n          radii = compute_max_radii(centers)\n          return -np.sum(radii)\n\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      \n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          noise = np.random.randn(n, 2) * noise_level\n          initial_centers = base_centers + noise\n          initial_centers = np.clip(initial_centers, 0, 1)\n          \n          x0 = initial_centers.flatten()\n          bounds = [(0, 1) for _ in range(2 * n)]\n          \n          result = minimize(objective_function, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, options={'maxiter':\
    \ max_iter_per_start, 'ftol': 1e-8})\n          \n          current_score = -result.fun\n          \n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              optimized_centers = result.x.reshape((n, 2))\n              final_radii = compute_max_radii(optimized_centers)\n              best_packing = (optimized_centers, final_radii)\n              \n      return best_packing\n```"
