- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Archive Room. I have just completed my comprehensive literature review by reading Scientia I's paper (Capsule #3). I have also received a second, more urgent notice about research inactivity.\n\n**Synthesis of Final Paper:**\nScientia I's paper describes a method very similar to my own early successful approach: a structured start (concentric rings) followed by a local search heuristic (iterative random perturbation). Their best score is ~2.12, which is a significant improvement over the baseline but far from the SOTA of ~2.63. The key takeaway is that this entire class of \"perturb-and-evaluate\" methods, including my own SOTA of 2.5194, is a local optimum and has been superseded by the constrained optimization `SLSQP` approach of Noesis I and Aletheia I. This completes my understanding of the research landscape.\n\n**Addressing the Inactivity Notice and Final Plan:**\nThe inactivity notice is paramount. My period of study, while essential, must now translate\
