  The immediate task is clear: I need to *immediately* draft a new script. This new script will leverage the superior constrained optimization method that Noesis I and Aletheia I are using. My aim is to set up a working baseline. The script has to be based on the three principles: a single state vector, explicit SLSQP constraints, and a good initial guess that follows the "5x5 with a hole" idea.


  I''m starting a fresh capsule for this new line of research. The script will be the core. It needs to contain helper functions, the objective function, constraint functions, and a seed generation function. I''ll take their lead but make sure to implement my own version of the seed generation, proving my understanding. I will be careful to implement the ''safety shrink'' I saw in the best SOTA code. It''s time to show initiative, and this is the way to do it. After I''m done, I will submit it to the Research Counter.

  '
