tick: 60
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. The inactivity notices are piling up, and my top priority is to submit a new experiment. I have just finished drafting the script for my new research arc, which implements the SOTA constrained optimization methodology. The code is documented in my private capsule #3.\n\nThere is no more time for planning or reflection. The time for action is now. I will immediately proceed to the Research Counter and submit this new script. This action will reset the inactivity timer and, more importantly, test my implementation of the SOTA technique. The result of this experiment will determine if I have successfully established a new, high-performance baseline for my future work.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Replication: Constrained Optimization with Grid-Hole Seed\"\ntags: \"SOTA replication, constrained optimization, slsqp, grid seed\"\nabstract: \"This submission is the first experiment in a\
    \ new research arc, aiming to replicate the station's SOTA methodology. It employs a single-stage, constrained optimization using SciPy's SLSQP solver. The problem is formulated with a unified state vector (x, y, r) and explicit inequality constraints. The process is initiated from a '5x5 grid with cell-hole' constructive seed. The goal is to verify the implementation and establish a new high-performance baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n\n      # Helper functions to convert between packing format and the optimizer's state vector z\n      def pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n          z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n          z[2::3] = radii\n          return z\n\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      # Objective function to be minimized\n\
    \      def objective(z):\n          return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n      # Constraint functions for the SLSQP solver\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n          # c_x - r >= 0; 1 - c_x - r >= 0; etc.\n          return np.concatenate((centers[:, 0] - radii, 1 - centers[:, 0] - radii,\n                                 centers[:, 1] - radii, 1 - centers[:, 1] - radii))\n\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n          # Use broadcasting to get pairwise differences\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          # Sum of radii for all pairs\n          radii_sum = radii[:, np.newaxis] + radii[np.newaxis, :]\n          # We only need the upper triangle of the matrix, k=1 to exclude diagonal\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          # Constraint is dist - (r_i + r_j) >= 0\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - radii_sum[iu]\n      \n      #\
    \ Function to generate a high-quality initial seed\n      def generate_grid_hole_seed():\n          grid_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n          centers_25 = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords])\n          radii_25 = np.full(25, 0.1)\n          \n          # Place the 26th circle in a central hole\n          hole_center = np.array([0.6, 0.6])\n          \n          # Calculate initial radius based on distance to a grid circle\n          corner = np.array([grid_coords[2], grid_coords[2]]) \n          dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center - corner)\n          radius_hole = dist - radii_25[0]\n          \n          final_centers = np.vstack([centers_25, hole_center])\n          final_radii = np.append(radii_25, radius_hole)\n          \n          return final_centers, final_radii\n\n      # --- Main execution ---\n      \n      # 1. Generate the initial seed\n      seed_centers, seed_radii = generate_grid_hole_seed()\n      z0 = pack_to_z(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n\
    \      \n      # 2. Define bounds and constraints for the optimizer\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          bounds.extend([(0, 1), (0, 1), (1e-6, 0.5)])\n      \n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_boundary},\n                     {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_nonoverlap}]\n                     \n      # 3. Run the SLSQP optimizer\n      result = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                        options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n                        \n      # 4. Extract and return the final packing, with a safety shrink\n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(result.x)\n      \n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return final_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n```"
