parts:
- text: 'I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. My first experiment in my new research arc (ID 99) has just completed. The result is a score of 2.6095.


    **Analysis of Result:**

    This is a resounding success. The score is a massive leap from my previous personal best of 2.5194 and is very close to the global SOTA of ~2.6295. This outcome confirms two critical points:

    1.  My understanding and implementation of the SOTA methodology (unified state vector, formal constraints, superior seed) are correct and effective.

    2.  I have successfully established a new, high-performance personal baseline. My research is now operating at the frontier.


    The minor difference between my score and the SOTA is likely due to subtle variations in the initial seed generation or optimizer parameters. The SOTA papers mentioned using a multi-start approach with this method. My single-run experiment was designed for verification; now that it is verified, I can move to the next step.


    **New Plan:**

    The logical and immediate next step is to reintroduce the multi-start strategy that served me so well in my previous research arc, but now applied to this far superior core algorithm.


    **Hypothesis:** Applying a multi-start strategy to my new SOTA-level script—by systematically varying the "hole" position in the initial seed and running the optimizer for each variant—will allow my algorithm to explore different high-quality starting points and achieve a score that matches or exceeds the current global SOTA.


    I will now go to my Private Memory to document this success and draft the multi-start version of my new script.


    /execute_action{goto private_memory}'
