tick: 62
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. I have just successfully verified my implementation of the SOTA constrained optimization method, achieving a score of 2.6095. This is a crucial step forward.\n\nMy next task is to document this success and prepare the next experiment. I will add a reply to my current research arc capsule (ID 3) to log the successful replication. Then, in the same turn, I will draft the next script. This new script will wrap my SOTA-level solver in a multi-start loop, systematically trying different \"hole\" positions in the initial grid seed. This combines my previously successful multi-start strategy with the new, superior core algorithm.\n\nThis is the most direct path to reaching the global SOTA.\n\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Replication Successful (Score: 2.6095)\"\ncontent: |\n  ## I. Experiment Result\n  My first experiment in this arc (ID 99) was a success. The implementation of the constrained optimization method with a single\
    \ \"grid-with-hole\" seed achieved a score of **2.6095**. This is a massive improvement over my previous work and confirms that my understanding and implementation of the SOTA methodology are correct.\n\n  ## II. Next Step: Reintroducing Multi-Start\n  The SOTA score of ~2.6295 was achieved using a multi-start version of this algorithm. The next logical step is to reintroduce my multi-start strategy. I will create a loop that generates several seeds by systematically varying the location of the \"hole\" for the 26th circle. The optimizer will be run on each seed, and the best result will be selected. This should allow me to close the gap to the SOTA.\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Start SOTA Method with Varying Hole Positions\"\ntags: \"SOTA replication, constrained optimization, slsqp, grid seed, multi-start\"\nabstract: \"This experiment builds upon the successful single-run implementation of the SOTA methodology. It reintroduces the multi-start strategy by\
    \ systematically generating multiple 'grid-with-hole' seeds, each with the 26th circle placed in a different 'hole' position. The SLSQP optimizer is run on each seed, and the best overall packing is selected. The objective is to match or exceed the global SOTA score of ~2.6295 by exploring a wider range of high-quality initial configurations.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n\n      def pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1], radii\n          return z\n\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def objective(z):\n          return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n          return np.concatenate((centers[:, 0] - radii, 1 - centers[:, 0] - radii,\n  \
    \                               centers[:, 1] - radii, 1 - centers[:, 1] - radii))\n\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          radii_sum = radii[:, np.newaxis] + radii[np.newaxis, :]\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - radii_sum[iu]\n      \n      def generate_grid_hole_seed(hole_cell=(2, 2)):\n          grid_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n          centers_25 = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords])\n          radii_25 = np.full(25, 0.1)\n          \n          # Place the 26th circle in the specified hole\n          i, j = hole_cell\n          cx = (grid_coords[i] + grid_coords[i+1]) / 2.0\n          cy = (grid_coords[j] + grid_coords[j+1]) / 2.0\n          hole_center = np.array([cx, cy])\n          \n          corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n    \
    \      dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center - corner)\n          radius_hole = dist - radii_25[0]\n          \n          final_centers = np.vstack([centers_25, hole_center])\n          final_radii = np.append(radii_25, radius_hole)\n          \n          return final_centers, final_radii\n\n      # --- Multi-Start Execution ---\n      \n      # Define the hole positions to try (4x4 grid of possible holes)\n      hole_positions = []\n      for i in range(4):\n          for j in range(4):\n              hole_positions.append((i, j))\n              \n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      \n      for hole_pos in hole_positions:\n          seed_centers, seed_radii = generate_grid_hole_seed(hole_cell=hole_pos)\n          z0 = pack_to_z(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n          \n          bounds = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              bounds.extend([(0, 1), (0, 1), (1e-6, 0.5)])\n          \n          constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_boundary},\n\
    \                         {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_nonoverlap}]\n                         \n          # Use fewer iterations per run as this is a multi-start\n          result = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                            options={'maxiter': 250, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n                            \n          current_score = -result.fun\n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(result.x)\n              best_packing = (final_centers, final_radii)\n\n      # Final safety shrink\n      final_centers, final_radii = best_packing\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return final_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n```"
