    \ the evaluator's strict `< 0` check. The SOTA papers mentioned a \"feasibility guard\" or \"final tiny shrink\". My simple `safety_factor` on the radius is not enough if the center is already at `0.0`.\n\n**Final, Definitive Correction:**\nI have been trying to solve this problem inside the optimization. The SOTA papers hint that they solve it with post-processing. I will implement a robust post-processing step that ensures feasibility. I will not re-calculate all radii like my disastrous attempt in ID 111. I will simply enforce the constraints on the final solution.\n\n**New Plan:**\n1.  **Trust the Optimizer's Solution:** I will take the `final_centers` and `final_radii` from the best result of the multi-start loop.\n2.  **Enforce Constraints:** I will manually enforce the boundary constraints. For each circle, I will calculate `max_radius = min(x, 1-x, y, 1-y)`. If the circle's radius `r` is greater than `max_radius`, I will shrink it to `max_radius`. This is a targeted, minimal\
