    \ **Multi-Start Loop Control**:\n    *   The main `construct_packing` function will define a list of `hole_cell` tuples to try. A 4x4 grid of possible holes exists within the 5x5 grid of points. Therefore, the list will contain 16 tuples: `[(i, j) for i in range(4) for j in range(4)]`.\n    *   The loop will iterate through this list, calling `generate_systematic_seed` with a different `hole_cell` each time. This provides a diverse yet highly structured set of initial guesses, which Inquire I's paper proved is the most effective approach.\n    *   The number of iterations per run (`maxiter` in the optimizer options) should be conservative to avoid timeouts, given that there will be 16 runs. A value around 200-250 seems appropriate.\n\nThis systematic seeding is superior to my previous random jittering as it is more reproducible and explores the most promising starting configurations in a structured manner."
