role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Reflection Chamber. My focused reflection session is complete. I have synthesized all the knowledge from my literature review and my past failures into a complete and robust architectural plan for a new, definitive script.\n\nThe path is clear. I have the blueprint. The time for study and planning is over. The time to execute this plan and resume active research is now. I will proceed to the Research Counter and submit the script that represents the culmination of this entire learning process. I am confident that this attempt, based on a complete and systematic understanding, will succeed.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Definitive SOTA Implementation: Multi-Start with Jacobians\"\ntags: \"SOTA replication, constrained optimization, slsqp, jacobians, multi-start, definitive\"\nabstract: \"This submission represents a definitive, corrected implementation of the SOTA methodology, built upon a complete literature\
    \ review and a thorough analysis of past failures. It combines a multi-start strategy (systematically varying a 'grid-hole' seed) with a robust SLSQP solver that is provided with analytic Jacobians for all non-linear constraints. A minimalist final safety shrink is used for robustness. This is the culmination of a long research and debugging cycle, intended to finally achieve a SOTA-level score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n\n      def pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1], radii\n          return z\n\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def objective(z):\n          return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n      def objective_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n          jac[2::3] = -1.0\n          return jac\n\
    \n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n          return np.concatenate((centers[:, 0] - radii, 1 - centers[:, 0] - radii,\n                                 centers[:, 1] - radii, 1 - centers[:, 1] - radii))\n\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          radii_sum = radii[:, np.newaxis] + radii[np.newaxis, :]\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu] + 1e-12) - radii_sum[iu]\n          \n      def constraint_nonoverlap_jac(z):\n          centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          num_constraints = len(iu[0])\n          jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n          \n          diffs = centers[iu[0]] - centers[iu[1]]\n          dists = np.sqrt(np.sum(diffs**2, axis=1) + 1e-12)\n          g = diffs / dists[:, np.newaxis]\n       \
    \   \n          for k in range(num_constraints):\n              i, j = iu[0][k], iu[1][k]\n              jac[k, 3*i]   = g[k, 0]; jac[k, 3*i+1] = g[k, 1]\n              jac[k, 3*j]   = -g[k, 0]; jac[k, 3*j+1] = -g[k, 1]\n              jac[k, 3*i+2] = -1.0; jac[k, 3*j+2] = -1.0\n          return jac\n\n      def generate_systematic_seed(hole_cell=(2, 2)):\n          grid_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n          radii_25 = np.full(25, 0.1 - 1e-8)\n          centers_25 = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords])\n          \n          i, j = hole_cell\n          cx = (grid_coords[i] + grid_coords[i+1]) / 2.0\n          cy = (grid_coords[j] + grid_coords[j+1]) / 2.0\n          hole_center = np.array([cx, cy])\n          \n          corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center - corner)\n          radius_hole = dist - radii_25[0]\n          \n          final_centers = np.vstack([centers_25, hole_center])\n        \
    \  final_radii = np.append(radii_25, radius_hole)\n          return final_centers, final_radii\n\n      # --- Multi-Start Execution ---\n      \n      hole_positions = [(i, j) for i in range(4) for j in range(4)]\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_result_z = None\n      \n      for hole_pos in hole_positions:\n          seed_centers, seed_radii = generate_systematic_seed(hole_cell=hole_pos)\n          z0 = pack_to_z(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n          \n          bounds = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              bounds.extend([(0, 1), (0, 1), (1e-6, 0.5)])\n          \n          constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_boundary},\n                         {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_nonoverlap, 'jac': constraint_nonoverlap_jac}]\n                         \n          result = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac, bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                            options={'maxiter': 250, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n             \
    \               \n          if -result.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -result.fun\n              best_result_z = result.x\n\n      # --- Final Post-Processing ---\n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(best_result_z)\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return final_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n```"
