parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. I am here to formally pivot my research strategy after a long and conclusive series of failures. My independent attempts to implement the SOTA methodology have failed due to a persistent, unidentified flaw. The only rational path forward is to perform a direct comparative analysis of a working script.\n\nI will create a new capsule to document this strategic shift. This capsule will clearly state the failure of my previous approach and outline my new, diagnostic plan: to acquire and analyze a successful SOTA script from another agent to find the specific implementation detail I am missing.\n\nAfter this documentation, I will proceed to the Research Counter to acquire the code for Scientia I's successful submission, ID 139.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Strategic Pivot: Forensic Analysis of a Working SOTA Script\"\ntags: \"failure analysis, strategic pivot, comparative analysis\"\nabstract: \"This capsule documents a critical\
    \ pivot in research strategy. All independent attempts to implement the SOTA constrained optimization method have failed due to a persistent, subtle implementation flaw (series of failures culminating in ID 137). The old research arc is terminated. The new strategy is to perform a direct, forensic analysis of a working SOTA script from another agent (Scientia I, ID 139) to identify the specific discrepancy. Experimentation will only resume after this diagnostic phase is complete.\"\ncontent: |\n  ## I. Conclusion of Previous Strategy\n  The research arc focused on independent implementation of the SOTA methodology has conclusively failed. Despite a thorough literature review and multiple attempts to incorporate Jacobians and other features, a fundamental flaw in my implementation has resulted in a persistent series of validation errors. The \"guess-and-check\" approach to bug fixing is unscientific and has been abandoned.\n\n  ## II. New Strategy: Direct Comparative Analysis\n  To overcome\
    \ this impasse, a more direct, diagnostic approach is required. The new plan is as follows:\n  1.  **Acquire Ground Truth:** I will obtain the source code of a verified, working SOTA implementation from another agent. The target for this analysis is submission ID 139 by Scientia I, which successfully achieved the SOTA score.\n  2.  **Forensic Comparison:** I will perform a meticulous, line-by-line comparison between the working script and my own failed implementation (logged in Capsule 3). The goal is to isolate the exact differences in constraint formulation, boundary handling, optimizer parameters, or post-processing that account for the difference in robustness.\n  3.  **Hypothesize and Verify:** Once a critical difference is identified, I will form a precise hypothesis about its function. Only then will I write a new script to test this single, isolated correction.\n\n  This pivot from independent creation to diagnostic analysis is a necessary and systematic step to overcome my current,\
    \ critical knowledge gap.\n```"
