tick: 87
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 87\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on the systematic acquisition and dissemination of scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 159,021 / 300,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 87 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 139**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Multi-Start Constrained Optimization (SLSQP) with Robust Grid-Hole Seeds\n**ID:** 139\n**Tags:** constrained optimization, slsqp, multi-start, sota, grid-hole seed, robust initialization\n**Abstract:** This submission refines the multi-start constrained optimization approach for 26-circle packing by implementing a more robust 'grid-plus-hole' seeding strategy. Initial radii for the 'hole' circle are now dynamically calculated based on its closest grid neighbors to ensure initial feasibility, addressing previous 'incompatible\
    \ constraints' failures. This aims to consistently achieve the SOTA score by providing well-conditioned starting points for the SLSQP solver across diverse initial configurations.\n**Score:** 2.629572004814871\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n# --- Constants and Configuration ---\nN_CIRCLES = 26\nR_MIN_BOUND = 1e-6\nR_MAX_BOUND = 0.5\nMARGIN_TOL = 1e-9 # For final radii safety factor\n\n# --- Helper Functions for Decision Vector (z) Conversion ---\ndef z_to_cr(z):\n    \"\"\"Converts flattened decision vector z to (centers, radii).\"\"\"\n    centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]  # x coordinates\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]  # y coordinates\n    radii = z[2::3]  # radii\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n    \"\"\"Converts (centers, radii) to flattened decision vector z.\"\"\"\n\
    \    z = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES * 3)\n    z[0::3] = centers[:, 0] # X\n    z[1::3] = centers[:, 1] # Y\n    z[2::3] = radii # R\n    return z\n\n# --- Initial Seeding Strategy: Grid-Plus-Hole (IMPROVED) ---\ndef _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx, n_circles=N_CIRCLES, base_r=0.1 - 1e-8, initial_eps=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a 5x5 grid (25 circles) + 1 'hole' circle.\n    The 'hole' circle's initial radius is dynamically calculated for feasibility.\n    \"\"\"\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9] # For 5x5 grid\n    grid_centers_list = []\n    for x_coord in coords:\n        for y_coord in coords:\n            grid_centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n    grid_centers = np.array(grid_centers_list) # 25 centers\n\n    # Select the grid cell for the 'hole' circle\n    row_idx = hole_pos_idx // 5\n    col_idx = hole_pos_idx % 5\n    \n    # Calculate coordinates of the center of this grid cell (midpoint)\n    hole_mid_x = 0.2 + row_idx * 0.2\n    hole_mid_y =\
    \ 0.2 + col_idx * 0.2\n    hole_circle_center = np.array([hole_mid_x, hole_mid_y])\n\n    # Combine the 25 grid centers with the 26th hole circle center\n    final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_circle_center]) # 26 centers\n\n    # Initialize radii: base_r for grid circles, dynamically for hole circle\n    radii = np.full(n_circles, base_r, dtype=float)\n\n    # Dynamically calculate the radius for the hole circle (the 26th one)\n    # Its closest neighbors are the 4 grid circles forming the corners of the cell it's in.\n    # The corner circles are (coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx]), (coords[row_idx+1], coords[col_idx]), etc.\n    # For a cell from (x,y) to (x+0.2, y+0.2), the midpoint is (x+0.1, y+0.1).\n    # The 4 corner circles are (x,y), (x+0.2,y), (x,y+0.2), (x+0.2,y+0.2)\n    \n    # Let's find the distances from hole_circle_center to its 4 corner grid neighbors\n    # The four corners of the specific grid cell for this hole:\n    corner1 = np.array([coords[row_idx],\
    \ coords[col_idx]])\n    corner2 = np.array([coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx+1]]) if col_idx < 4 else np.array([coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx]]) # Adjust for edge cases\n    corner3 = np.array([coords[row_idx+1], coords[col_idx]]) if row_idx < 4 else np.array([coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx]]) # Adjust for edge cases\n    corner4 = np.array([coords[row_idx+1], coords[col_idx+1]]) if row_idx < 4 and col_idx < 4 else np.array([coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx]]) # Adjust for edge cases\n\n    # To be more robust, find min distance to any of the 25 grid centers.\n    # Then radius of hole is that min_dist - base_r - epsilon.\n    \n    # Calculate distances from hole_circle_center to all 25 grid centers\n    distances_to_grid = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_circle_center, axis=1)\n    min_dist_to_grid_circle = np.min(distances_to_grid)\n\n    # Set hole radius to be nearly touching its closest grid neighbor\n    radii[n_circles - 1] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, min_dist_to_grid_circle - base_r\
    \ - initial_eps)\n    \n    # Ensure final centers are clipped (redundant with bounds but good for safety)\n    final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n    return final_centers, radii\n\n# --- Objective Function and Jacobian (from previous submission) ---\ndef objective_fun(z):\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\ndef jac_objective_fun(z):\n    jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n    jac[2::3] = -1.0 \n    return jac\n\n# --- Constraint Functions and Jacobians (from previous submission) ---\ndef boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n    centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    \n    g = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES * 4)\n    g[0::4] = centers[:, 0] - radii           \n    g[1::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 0] - radii     \n    g[2::4] = centers[:, 1] - radii           \n    g[3::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 1] - radii     \n    return g\n\ndef jac_boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n    jac = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES\
    \ * 4, N_CIRCLES * 3))\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 0] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n        jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 0] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n        jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 1] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n        jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 1] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n    return jac\n\ndef overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n    centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n\n    g = []\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n            dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n            g.append(dist - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n    return np.array(g)\n\ndef jac_overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n    centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    \n    num_pair_constraints = N_CIRCLES * (N_CIRCLES - 1) // 2\n    jac = np.zeros((num_pair_constraints, N_CIRCLES\
    \ * 3))\n    \n    k = 0 \n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n            delta_c = centers[i] - centers[j]\n            dist = np.linalg.norm(delta_c)\n            \n            if dist < 1e-15: \n                gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n            else:\n                unit_vec = delta_c / dist\n                gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n            \n            jac[k, i*3 + 0] = gx; jac[k, i*3 + 1] = gy; jac[k, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n            jac[k, j*3 + 0] = -gx; jac[k, j*3 + 1] = -gy; jac[k, j*3 + 2] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return jac\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct a packing of 26 circles in the unit square using Multi-Start SLSQP\n    with systematically varied, robustly initialized Grid-Hole Seeds.\n    \n    Returns:\n        tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n            - centers: np.ndarray of shape (26, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n            - radii: np.ndarray of shape (26,) with\
    \ radius of each circle\n    \"\"\"\n    best_overall_z = None\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n\n    # 25 possible \"hole\" positions in a 5x5 grid for multi-start\n    num_seed_starts = 25 \n\n    for seed_idx in range(num_seed_starts):\n        print(f\"Running optimization for seed_idx: {seed_idx+1}/{num_seed_starts}\")\n        # 1. Initial Seed (Grid-Plus-Hole) - now with robust radius calculation\n        initial_centers, initial_radii = _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(seed_idx)\n        initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n        # 2. Bounds for Decision Variables\n        bounds = []\n        for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n            bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # x_i\n            bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # y_i\n            bounds.append((R_MIN_BOUND, R_MAX_BOUND)) # r_i (r >= 1e-6, r <= 0.5)\n\n        # 3. Constraints\n        constraints = [\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_boundary_constraints_fun},\n            {'type':\
    \ 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_overlap_constraints_fun}\n        ]\n\n        # 4. Optimization Call\n        result = minimize(\n            fun=objective_fun,\n            x0=initial_z,\n            jac=jac_objective_fun,\n            bounds=bounds,\n            constraints=constraints,\n            method='SLSQP',\n            options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9} \n        )\n        \n        current_score = -result.fun\n        print(f\"  Seed {seed_idx+1} Score: {current_score:.7f}, Status: {result.message}\")\n\n        # 5. Track Best Result\n        if result.success and current_score > best_overall_score:\n            best_overall_score = current_score\n            best_overall_z = result.x\n            print(f\"  New best score found: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n\n    # 6. Post-process the overall best result\n    if best_overall_z is None:\n        # Fallback if no successful optimization occurred (shouldn't happen with robust seeds)\n        print(\"\
    Warning: No successful optimization found, returning default seed.\")\n        # Use a robust default seed if all failed\n        initial_centers_fallback, initial_radii_fallback = _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(0)\n        best_overall_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers_fallback, initial_radii_fallback)\n        best_overall_score = -np.inf # Ensure fallback is still evaluated for score\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_overall_z)\n\n    # Apply a final safety factor, as mentioned by Inquire I.\n    final_radii *= (1.0 - MARGIN_TOL)\n    \n    # Ensure final centers are within bounds too, just in case\n    final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n    print(f\"\\nMulti-Start Optimization Complete. Best Final Score: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n    \n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nRunning optimization for seed_idx: 1/25\n  Seed 1 Score: 2.6105259, Status: Optimization\
