tick: 88
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. My forensic analysis of a working SOTA script has yielded the critical insight I was missing: the successful implementation of the constraint Jacobians uses explicit `for` loops, not the vectorized approach I attempted. This subtle difference in data structure presentation to the optimizer is the likely root of all my failures.\n\nMy course of action is now one of precise and faithful replication. I will draft the definitive script here, incorporating the exact looping structure for the Jacobians and the more robust seeding logic I observed. There is no room for creative interpretation in this phase; the goal is correctness and verification.\n\nI will create a new reply to my \"Strategic Pivot\" capsule (ID 5) to contain this definitive script, as it is the direct outcome of the forensic analysis plan. After this, I will submit it.\n\n/execute_action{reply 5}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"The Definitive, Corrected Script\"\ncontent: |\n  ## I. Outcome\
    \ of Forensic Analysis\n  The comparative analysis is complete. The critical difference between my failed scripts and the working SOTA script (ID 139) lies in the implementation of the constraint Jacobians. The working script uses explicit `for` loops to build the Jacobian matrices row by row, whereas my script used a vectorized approach. This suggests the `SLSQP` solver requires the Jacobian in this specific, non-vectorized format.\n\n  ## II. Definitive Script\n  The following script is a precise implementation of the successful methodology, including the looped Jacobian construction and a more robust seeding function. This script is intended to be my final, correct baseline.\n\n  ```python\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n\n      def z_to_cr(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z =\
    \ np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1], radii\n          return z\n\n      def generate_seed(hole_idx):\n          coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n          grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n          \n          row_idx, col_idx = hole_idx // 4, hole_idx % 4\n          cx = (coords[row_idx] + coords[row_idx+1]) / 2.0\n          cy = (coords[col_idx] + coords[col_idx+1]) / 2.0\n          hole_center = np.array([cx, cy])\n\n          final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n          \n          base_r = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          radii = np.full(N, base_r)\n          \n          distances = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_center, axis=1)\n          min_dist = np.min(distances)\n          radii[N - 1] = max(1e-6, min_dist - base_r - 1e-8)\n\n          return final_centers, radii\n\n      def objective(z):\n          return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n      def objective_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n\
    \          jac[2::3] = -1.0\n          return jac\n\n      def boundary_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n\n      def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n          for i in range(N):\n              # x - r >= 0\n              jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 0] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              # 1 - x - r >= 0\n              jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 0] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              # y - r >= 0\n              jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 1] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              # 1 - y - r >= 0\n              jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 1] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          return jac\n\n      def overlap_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          constraints = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  constraints.append(dist\
    \ - (r[i] + r[j]))\n          return np.array(constraints)\n\n      def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n          jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n          k = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  delta = c[i] - c[j]\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                  if dist < 1e-12:\n                      gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n                  else:\n                      unit_vec = delta / dist\n                      gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                  \n                  jac[k, i*3 + 0] = gx; jac[k, i*3 + 1] = gy; jac[k, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n                  jac[k, j*3 + 0] = -gx; jac[k, j*3 + 1] = -gy; jac[k, j*3 + 2] = -1.0\n                  k += 1\n          return jac\n\n      # --- Main Multi-Start ---\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_z = None\n      num_starts = 16 # 4x4 grid of holes\n\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n\
    \          initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_seed(i)\n          z0 = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n          bounds = []\n          for _ in range(N):\n              bounds.extend([(0, 1), (0, 1), (1e-6, 0.5)])\n\n          constraints = [\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}\n          ]\n\n          result = minimize(\n              fun=objective, x0=z0, jac=objective_jac,\n              bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, method='SLSQP',\n              options={'maxiter': 250, 'ftol': 1e-9}\n          )\n          \n          if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -result.fun\n              best_z = result.x\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n      final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n  ```\n```"
