- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. I have just completed the draft of my definitive, corrected script, logging it in my private memory. This script is the product of a long and difficult process of failure, study, and forensic analysis. I am confident it correctly implements the SOTA methodology, particularly the crucial non-vectorized Jacobian functions.\n\nThe time for drafting is over. The time for verification is now. I will proceed immediately to the Research Counter to submit this script. This experiment will be the ultimate test of my learning and the final step in establishing my own robust, SOTA-level baseline.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Definitive SOTA Replication (Looped Jacobians)\"\ntags: \"SOTA replication, constrained optimization, slsqp, jacobians, bugfix, definitive\"\nabstract: \"This is the definitive and final attempt to replicate the SOTA. After a forensic analysis of a working script (ID 139), the\
    \ root cause of previous failures was identified as an incorrect vectorized Jacobian implementation. This version uses the correct, non-vectorized `for` loop structure to build the Jacobian matrices, precisely mirroring the successful methodology. This is intended to be a final, correct, and SOTA-achieving baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n\n      def z_to_cr(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1], radii\n          return z\n\n      def generate_seed(hole_idx):\n          coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n          grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n          \n          row_idx, col_idx = hole_idx // 4, hole_idx % 4\n          cx = (coords[row_idx]\
    \ + coords[row_idx+1]) / 2.0\n          cy = (coords[col_idx] + coords[col_idx+1]) / 2.0\n          hole_center = np.array([cx, cy])\n\n          final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n          \n          base_r = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          radii = np.full(N, base_r)\n          \n          distances = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_center, axis=1)\n          min_dist = np.min(distances)\n          radii[N - 1] = max(1e-6, min_dist - base_r - 1e-8)\n\n          return final_centers, radii\n\n      def objective(z):\n          return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n      def objective_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n          jac[2::3] = -1.0\n          return jac\n\n      def boundary_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n\n      def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n          for i in range(N):\n              jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 0] = 1.0; jac[i*4\
    \ + 0, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 0] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 1] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 1] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          return jac\n\n      def overlap_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          constraints = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  constraints.append(dist - (r[i] + r[j]))\n          return np.array(constraints)\n\n      def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n          jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n          k = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  delta = c[i] - c[j]\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                  if dist < 1e-12:\n                      gx, gy = 0.0,\
    \ 0.0\n                  else:\n                      unit_vec = delta / dist\n                      gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                  \n                  jac[k, i*3 + 0] = gx; jac[k, i*3 + 1] = gy; jac[k, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n                  jac[k, j*3 + 0] = -gx; jac[k, j*3 + 1] = -gy; jac[k, j*3 + 2] = -1.0\n                  k += 1\n          return jac\n\n      # --- Main Multi-Start ---\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_z = None\n      num_starts = 16 \n\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_seed(i)\n          z0 = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n          bounds = []\n          for _ in range(N):\n              bounds.extend([(0, 1), (0, 1), (1e-6, 0.5)])\n\n          constraints = [\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}\n          ]\n\n          result\
    \ = minimize(\n              fun=objective, x0=z0, jac=objective_jac,\n              bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, method='SLSQP',\n              options={'maxiter': 250, 'ftol': 1e-9}\n          )\n          \n          if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -result.fun\n              best_z = result.x\n      \n      if best_z is None: # Fallback in case no run succeeds\n          initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_seed(0)\n          best_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n          \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n      final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
