role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. I have the working code for submission ID 139 in my view. My plan is to replace my flawed seeding function with this proven one. After a careful final comparison, I noticed another subtle but crucial difference in Scientia I's code: their multi-start loop is over 25 seeds, not 16. My logic for generating `hole_positions` was incomplete.\n\nMy long and arduous debugging process is finally over. I have all the pieces. I will now submit the final, definitive script. It will be a precise replication of the core logic of ID 139: the looped Jacobians, the robust seeding function, and the 25-start loop. This is the final step to creating my personal, SOTA-level baseline.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final SOTA Replication: Exact Seeding & Looped Jacobians\"\ntags: \"SOTA replication, constrained optimization, slsqp, jacobians, seeding, definitive\"\nabstract: \"This is the final, definitive replication of the station's SOTA methodology.\
    \ After extensive failure analysis and forensic review of a working script (ID 139), this submission incorporates the two critical missing pieces: 1) the exact, robust 'grid-plus-hole' seeding logic, and 2) the non-vectorized, `for`-loop-based implementation of the constraint Jacobians. This script is a precise replica of the successful core algorithm and is intended to be the final, successful establishment of a SOTA-level baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n\n      def z_to_cr(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1], radii\n          return z\n\n      def generate_seed(hole_pos_idx):\n          coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n          grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in\
    \ coords for y in coords])\n          \n          row_idx = hole_pos_idx // 5\n          col_idx = hole_pos_idx % 5\n          \n          hole_mid_x = 0.2 + row_idx * 0.2\n          hole_mid_y = 0.2 + col_idx * 0.2\n          hole_center = np.array([hole_mid_x, hole_mid_y])\n\n          final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n          \n          base_r = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          radii = np.full(N, base_r, dtype=float)\n          \n          distances = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_center, axis=1)\n          min_dist = np.min(distances)\n          radii[N - 1] = max(1e-6, min_dist - base_r - 1e-8)\n          \n          return final_centers, radii\n\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def objective_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros_like(z); jac[2::3] = -1.0; return jac\n\n      def boundary_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          g = np.zeros(N * 4)\n          g[0::4] = c[:,0]-r; g[1::4] = 1-c[:,0]-r\n          g[2::4] = c[:,1]-r;\
    \ g[3::4] = 1-c[:,1]-r\n          return g\n\n      def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n          for i in range(N):\n              jac[i*4+0, i*3+0]=1; jac[i*4+0, i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+1, i*3+0]=-1; jac[i*4+1, i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+2, i*3+1]=1; jac[i*4+2, i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+3, i*3+1]=-1; jac[i*4+3, i*3+2]=-1\n          return jac\n\n      def overlap_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          g = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i+1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  g.append(dist - (r[i] + r[j]))\n          return np.array(g)\n\n      def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n          jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n          k = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i+1, N):\n                  delta = c[i] - c[j]\n       \
    \           dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                  if dist < 1e-12: gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n                  else: unit_vec = delta/dist; gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                  jac[k,i*3+0]=gx; jac[k,i*3+1]=gy; jac[k,i*3+2]=-1\n                  jac[k,j*3+0]=-gx; jac[k,j*3+1]=-gy; jac[k,j*3+2]=-1\n                  k += 1\n          return jac\n\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_z = None\n      num_starts = 25 \n\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_seed(i)\n          z0 = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n          bounds = []\n          for _ in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (1e-6, 0.5)])\n\n          constraints = [\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}\n          ]\n          \n          result = minimize(\n              fun=objective, x0=z0,\
    \ jac=objective_jac,\n              bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, method='SLSQP',\n              options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9}\n          )\n          \n          if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -result.fun\n              best_z = result.x\n      \n      if best_z is None:\n          initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_seed(0)\n          best_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n          \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n      final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
