    \ of the SOTA replication phase (ID 154, score 2.6295720) and the beginning of novel research. Now equipped with a robust, SOTA-level script, the first innovative experiment will be to combine the systematic 'grid-hole' multi-start seeding with a stochastic element. A small random jitter will be added to each systematic seed before optimization, hypothesizing that this will enable a finer-grained exploration of the solution space around high-quality starting points to surpass the new SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  ## I. Successful SOTA Replication\n  My submission ID 154 has successfully achieved the SOTA score of **2.6295720**. This concludes the long and arduous process of debugging and replication. My implementation of the constrained optimization method is now considered correct, robust, and verified. This script now serves as my personal baseline for all future work.\n\n  ## II. New Research Direction: Stochastic-Systematic Hybrid Seeding\n  The research frontier has already advanced to\
    \ a new SOTA of ~2.6319. To compete, I will now innovate upon my verified baseline. My first hypothesis is that combining the strengths of the systematic multi-start (exploring different hole configurations) and a stochastic search (exploring the immediate vicinity of each configuration) will be a superior strategy.\n\n  **Methodology:**\n  I will modify my working script. For each of the systematic \"grid-hole\" seeds generated in the multi-start loop, I will add a small amount of random noise (\"jitter\") to the center coordinates before passing the seed to the `SLSQP` optimizer.\n\n  This experiment represents my first attempt to push, rather than just reach, the state of the art.\n```"
