parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. I have documented my success and outlined my first innovative experiment. It is now time to execute this plan.\n\nI will proceed to the Research Counter and submit my new \"Jittered Multi-Start\" script. This is my first attempt to advance the SOTA, and it represents a synthesis of my own successful past methods with the more robust framework I have learned from the community.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Innovation 1: Jittered Multi-Start SOTA Method\"\ntags: \"SOTA, innovation, multi-start, stochastic, jitter, slsqp\"\nabstract: \"This is a first attempt to advance the SOTA. Building upon a now-correct SOTA replication script, this experiment reintroduces a stochastic element. A small random 'jitter' is added to each of the systematically generated 'grid-hole' seeds before optimization. The hypothesis is that this hybrid stochastic-systematic approach will enable a finer-grained exploration\
    \ of the solution space around each high-quality starting point, potentially discovering a packing that surpasses the current SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n\n      def z_to_cr(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1], radii\n          return z\n\n      def generate_seed(hole_pos_idx):\n          coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n          grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n          \n          row_idx = hole_pos_idx // 5\n          col_idx = hole_pos_idx % 5\n          \n          hole_mid_x = 0.2 + row_idx * 0.2\n          hole_mid_y = 0.2 + col_idx * 0.2\n          hole_center = np.array([hole_mid_x, hole_mid_y])\n\n          final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers,\
    \ hole_center])\n          \n          base_r = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          radii = np.full(N, base_r, dtype=float)\n          \n          distances = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_center, axis=1)\n          min_dist = np.min(distances)\n          radii[N - 1] = max(1e-6, min_dist - base_r - 1e-8)\n          \n          return final_centers, radii\n\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def objective_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros_like(z); jac[2::3] = -1.0; return jac\n\n      def boundary_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n\n      def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n          for i in range(N):\n              jac[i*4+0,i*3+0]=1; jac[i*4+0,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+1,i*3+0]=-1; jac[i*4+1,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+2,i*3+1]=1; jac[i*4+2,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+3,i*3+1]=-1; jac[i*4+3,i*3+2]=-1\n          return jac\n\
    \n      def overlap_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          g = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i+1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  g.append(dist - (r[i] + r[j]))\n          return np.array(g)\n\n      def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n          jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n          k = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i+1, N):\n                  delta = c[i] - c[j]\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                  if dist < 1e-12: gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n                  else: unit_vec = delta/dist; gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                  jac[k,i*3+0]=gx; jac[k,i*3+1]=gy; jac[k,i*3+2]=-1\n                  jac[k,j*3+0]=-gx; jac[k,j*3+1]=-gy; jac[k,j*3+2]=-1\n                  k += 1\n          return jac\n\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_z = None\n\
    \      num_starts = 25\n      jitter_magnitude = 0.005 # Small random noise\n\n      np.random.seed(96) # New seed for this new method\n\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_seed(i)\n          \n          # ** THE INNOVATION IS HERE **\n          # Add jitter to the systematic seed\n          noise = np.random.uniform(-jitter_magnitude, jitter_magnitude, size=initial_centers.shape)\n          initial_centers += noise\n          \n          z0 = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n          bounds = []\n          for _ in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (1e-6, 0.5)])\n\n          constraints = [\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}\n          ]\n          \n          result = minimize(\n              fun=objective, x0=z0, jac=objective_jac,\n              bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\
    \ method='SLSQP',\n              options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9}\n          )\n          \n          if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -result.fun\n              best_z = result.x\n      \n      if best_z is None:\n          initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_seed(0)\n          best_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n          \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n      final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
