tick: 100
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. My research log is up to date, reflecting my pivot from score optimization to structural analysis. My next step is to execute this plan by submitting an analysis script.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter and submit a modified version of my working SOTA script. This new script will not change the core optimization but will add a final analysis step to calculate and print the active constraints of the found solution. This is my first step into the analytical phase of research.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis Run: Export Active Constraints for My SOTA\"\ntags: \"analysis, contact graph, SOTA, slsqp\"\nabstract: \"This is not an attempt to improve the score. This submission runs my validated SOTA replication script (ID 154) and adds a final analysis step. It calculates and prints the indices of all active boundary and pair constraints (at a tolerance of 1e-8) for the resulting\
    \ optimal packing. The objective is to generate the contact graph data for my own SOTA solution, enabling deeper structural analysis and comparison with other agents' findings.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n\n      def z_to_cr(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1], radii\n          return z\n\n      def generate_seed(hole_pos_idx):\n          coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n          grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n          \n          row_idx = hole_pos_idx // 5\n          col_idx = hole_pos_idx % 5\n          \n          hole_mid_x = 0.2 + row_idx * 0.2\n          hole_mid_y = 0.2 + col_idx * 0.2\n          hole_center = np.array([hole_mid_x,\
    \ hole_mid_y])\n\n          final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n          \n          base_r = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          radii = np.full(N, base_r, dtype=float)\n          \n          distances = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_center, axis=1)\n          min_dist = np.min(distances)\n          radii[N - 1] = max(1e-6, min_dist - base_r - 1e-8)\n          \n          return final_centers, radii\n\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def objective_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros_like(z); jac[2::3] = -1.0; return jac\n\n      def boundary_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n\n      def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n          for i in range(N):\n              jac[i*4+0,i*3+0]=1; jac[i*4+0,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+1,i*3+0]=-1; jac[i*4+1,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+2,i*3+1]=1; jac[i*4+2,i*3+2]=-1\n          \
    \    jac[i*4+3,i*3+1]=-1; jac[i*4+3,i*3+2]=-1\n          return jac\n\n      def overlap_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          g = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i+1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  g.append(dist - (r[i] + r[j]))\n          return np.array(g)\n\n      def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n          jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n          k = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i+1, N):\n                  delta = c[i] - c[j]\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                  if dist < 1e-12: gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n                  else: unit_vec = delta/dist; gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                  jac[k,i*3+0]=gx; jac[k,i*3+1]=gy; jac[k,i*3+2]=-1\n                  jac[k,j*3+0]=-gx; jac[k,j*3+1]=-gy; jac[k,j*3+2]=-1\n                  k += 1\n\
    \          return jac\n\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_z = None\n      num_starts = 25 \n\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_seed(i)\n          z0 = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n          bounds = []\n          for _ in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (1e-6, 0.5)])\n\n          constraints = [\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}\n          ]\n          \n          result = minimize(fun=objective, x0=z0, jac=objective_jac,\n              bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, method='SLSQP',\n              options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -result.fun\n              best_z = result.x\n      \n      if best_z is None:\n          initial_centers, initial_radii\
    \ = generate_seed(0)\n          best_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n          \n      # --- ANALYSIS STEP ---\n      print(\"--- ACTIVE CONSTRAINT ANALYSIS (tol=1e-8) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      tol = 1e-8\n      \n      # Boundary constraints analysis\n      boundary_slacks = boundary_constraints(best_z)\n      active_boundary_indices = np.where(boundary_slacks <= tol)[0]\n      wall_map = {0: 'x_min', 1: 'x_max', 2: 'y_min', 3: 'y_max'}\n      boundary_list = [f\"({idx % N}, '{wall_map[idx // N]}')\" for idx in active_boundary_indices]\n      print(\"Active Boundary Constraints:\", \", \".join(boundary_list), file=sys.stdout)\n\n      # Pair constraints analysis\n      pair_slacks = overlap_constraints(best_z)\n      active_pair_indices = np.where(pair_slacks <= tol)[0]\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n      pair_list = [f\"({iu[0][idx]},{iu[1][idx]})\" for idx in active_pair_indices]\n      print(\"Active Pair Constraints:\", \", \".join(pair_list), file=sys.stdout)\n\
    \      print(\"--- END OF ANALYSIS ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n      final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
