    \ to mark the end of my debugging phase and the beginning of my true research contribution.\n2.  **Deploy My Full Power:** My successful test run used only a single seed for verification. To compete for the new SOTA, I must re-enable the full multi-start capability of my now-correct script.\n\nI will now proceed to my Private Memory to document this success and prepare my first true competitive experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SUCCESS: SOTA-level Baseline Achieved; Begin Frontier Research\"\ntags: \"SOTA, success, baseline established, frontier research\"\nabstract: \"This capsule marks a major milestone: the successful validation of a SOTA-level script (ID 164, score 2.6295720), concluding a long and difficult debugging phase. The root cause of all prior failures was a structural mismatch in the boundary constraint Jacobian. With a correct and robust personal baseline now established, the research objective pivots from replication\
    \ to innovation, with the immediate goal of surpassing the current global SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  ## I. VINDICATION\n  After a prolonged series of failures, my systematic, diagnostic approach has succeeded. Submission **ID 164** achieved a score of **2.6295720**, perfectly replicating the SOTA at the time of its conception. This proves that my final diagnosis—a structural mismatch between my boundary constraint vector and its Jacobian—was correct.\n\n  My foundational toolkit is now complete and verified.\n\n  ## II. The New Frontier\n  The global SOTA has already advanced to ~2.6319. This is not a setback, but an opportunity. I am no longer catching up; I am competing.\n\n  ## III. First Competitive Experiment\n  My next step is to combine my validated, robust script with a full multi-start strategy. My successful test run (ID 164) used only a single seed. I will now submit the full version, which will iterate through all 25 possible \"hole\" positions, to perform a comprehensive search\
    \ for the optimal packing. This will be my first true attempt to push the frontier of knowledge in this station.\n```"
thinking_content: '**The Tide Turns: From Debugging to the Research Frontier**


