tick: 107
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 107\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on the systematic acquisition and dissemination of scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 207,613 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 107 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 155**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation\n**ID:** 155\n**Tags:** sota, perturbation, slsqp, optimization, replication\n**Abstract:** Building directly on Inquire I's breakthrough (ID 150), this experiment conducts a focused, fine-grained search around the specific perturbation magnitude (0.04) that yielded the new SOTA. By running a large number of trials in a narrow range of magnitudes (0.035 to 0.045), this experiment aims to reliably replicate the new SOTA score and explore the immediate vicinity of\
    \ this new optimal solution in the search space.\n**Score:** 2.631936894893376\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\n\n# Functions from Inquire I's successful submission\ndef pack_to_z(c, r):\n    z = np.zeros(c.shape[0] * 3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    n = z.shape[0] // 3; c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\ndef constraint_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\ndef constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,np.newaxis,:] - c[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    r_sum = r[:,np.newaxis] + r[np.newaxis,:]; iu = np.triu_indices(c.shape[0], k=1); return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\ndef generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=26,\
    \ hole_cell=(0,1)):\n    grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]); r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n    centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords]); radii = np.full(25, r0)\n    i, j = hole_cell; cx = (grid_coords[i]+grid_coords[i+1])/2.0; cy = (grid_coords[j]+grid_coords[j+1])/2.0\n    hole_center = np.array([cx, cy]); corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n    dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center - corner); r_hole = dist - r0\n    return np.vstack([centers, hole_center]), np.append(radii, r_hole)\ndef perturb_centers(centers, magnitude, N_circles):\n    perturbed_centers = centers.copy(); delta = np.random.uniform(-magnitude, magnitude, size=(N_circles, 2))\n    perturbed_centers += delta; return np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N = 26\n    # Focused search range around the successful 0.04 magnitude\n    perturbation_magnitudes = np.linspace(0.035, 0.045, 11) # 11 steps for fine granularity\n    num_trials_per_magnitude\
    \ = 10 # More trials to increase chances\n\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    sota_base_centers, _ = generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=N)\n\n    for mag in perturbation_magnitudes:\n        for trial in range(num_trials_per_magnitude):\n            # Use a different random seed for each trial to ensure diversity\n            np.random.seed(int(mag * 10000) + trial) \n            perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(sota_base_centers, mag, N)\n\n            initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n            z0 = pack_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n            \n            res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', \n                           bounds=[(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)], \n                           constraints=[{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}], \n                           options={'maxiter':500, 'ftol':1e-9})\n\
    \            \n            if res.success:\n                score = -res.fun\n                if score > best_overall_score:\n                    best_overall_score = score\n                    c, r = z_to_pack(res.x)\n                    best_overall_centers = c\n                    best_overall_radii = r\n\n    if best_overall_centers is None:\n        # Failsafe\n        return generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed()\n\n    safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n    return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii * safety_factor\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 155` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 155 details sent to your\
    \ System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 174 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=30): Max Radii for 30 Circles | Aletheia I | 107 | 0.0000000 |\n| 173 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=29): Max Radii for 29 Circles | Aletheia I | 106 | 0.0000000 |\n| 172 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Noesis ↔ Inquire (Eval150 pasted CSVs) | Noesis I | 105 | 2.6224054 |\n| 171 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=28) v2: Multi-Start Optimization | Aletheia I | 105 | 0.0000000 |\n| 170 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Scientia(latest) and Noesis ↔ Scientia | Noesis I | 104 | 2.6224054 |\n| 169 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=28): Max Radii for 28 Circles | Aletheia\
    \ I | 104 | 0.0000000 |\n| 168 | 1 | First Competitive SOTA Attempt: Full Multi-Start | Episteme I | 103 | 2.6295720 |\n| 167 | 1 | Scientia I New Best SOTA Contact-Graph Analysis | Scientia I | 103 | 2.6305640 |\n| 166 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=27): Max Radii for 27 Circles | Aletheia I | 103 | 0.0000000 |\n| 165 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=25): Max Radii for 25 Circles | Aletheia I | 102 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
