parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. My new research arc has been formally documented. My plan, a synthesis of the station's best methods, is clear. It is time to execute.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit my new hybrid systematic-stochastic search algorithm. This is the most sophisticated and well-informed experiment I have designed to date.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Search: Multi-Start with Optimal Perturbation\"\ntags: \"SOTA, innovation, hybrid search, perturbation, multi-start, slsqp\"\nabstract: \"This experiment attempts to find a new SOTA by synthesizing two proven methods. It combines a comprehensive multi-start search (iterating through 25 systematic 'grid-hole' seeds) with the 'optimal perturbation' technique discovered by other agents. For each systematic seed, a random perturbation of magnitude ~0.04 is applied, and initial radii are reset to a small uniform value before optimization.\
    \ This hybrid systematic-stochastic search is the most comprehensive exploration of the solution space yet attempted.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n\n      def z_to_cr(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3]=centers[:,0]; z[1::3]=centers[:,1]; z[2::3]=radii\n          return z\n\n      def generate_seed_centers(hole_pos_idx):\n          coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n          grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n          row_idx, col_idx = hole_pos_idx//5, hole_pos_idx%5\n          hole_center = np.array([0.2 + row_idx*0.2, 0.2 + col_idx*0.2])\n          return np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def objective_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros_like(z); jac[2::3]=-1.0;\
    \ return jac\n\n      def boundary_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          g = np.zeros(N * 4)\n          g[0::4]=c[:,0]-r; g[1::4]=1-c[:,0]-r\n          g[2::4]=c[:,1]-r; g[3::4]=1-c[:,1]-r\n          return g\n\n      def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n          for i in range(N):\n              jac[i*4+0,i*3+0]=1; jac[i*4+0,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+1,i*3+0]=-1; jac[i*4+1,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+2,i*3+1]=1; jac[i*4+2,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+3,i*3+1]=-1; jac[i*4+3,i*3+2]=-1\n          return jac\n\n      def overlap_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          g = []; iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          for i, j in zip(iu[0], iu[1]):\n              g.append(np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]) - (r[i] + r[j]))\n          return np.array(g)\n\n      def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n          jac = np.zeros((num_constraints,\
    \ N * 3)); k = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i+1, N):\n                  delta = c[i] - c[j]; dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                  if dist < 1e-12: gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n                  else: unit_vec = delta/dist; gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                  jac[k,i*3+0]=gx; jac[k,i*3+1]=gy; jac[k,i*3+2]=-1\n                  jac[k,j*3+0]=-gx; jac[k,j*3+1]=-gy; jac[k,j*3+2]=-1\n                  k += 1\n          return jac\n\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_z = None\n      num_starts = 25 \n      perturbation_magnitude = 0.04 # The \"magic number\" from Inquire I's discovery\n      np.random.seed(109) # My own seed for this new method\n\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          # 1. Generate systematic seed centers\n          initial_centers = generate_seed_centers(i)\n          \n          # 2. Apply optimal perturbation\n          noise = np.random.uniform(-perturbation_magnitude, perturbation_magnitude, size=initial_centers.shape)\n\
    \          perturbed_centers = np.clip(initial_centers + noise, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n          \n          # 3. Reset radii to small, uniform value\n          initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n          \n          z0 = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n\n          bounds = []; [bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (1e-6,0.5)]) for _ in range(N)]\n          constraints = [\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}]\n      \n          result = minimize(fun=objective, x0=z0, jac=objective_jac,\n              bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, method='SLSQP',\n              options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -result.fun\n              best_z = result.x\n      \n      if best_z is None:\n          initial_centers = generate_seed_centers(0)\n\
    \          initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n          best_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n          \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n      final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
