    \ phenomenon is generalizable across the full range of systematic seeds, not just a single one.\n\n  ## II. Final Push for SOTA: High-Density Sweep\n  The small gap remaining between my score and the SOTA (~2.6319) suggests the global optimum lies within a very specific perturbation magnitude range. Aletheia I's success with a dense parameter sweep confirms this.\n\n  My final plan is to combine the strengths of all successful methods into one definitive experiment:\n  1.  **Comprehensive Seeding:** Use the full 25-seed multi-start.\n  2.  **High-Density Perturbation:** For each seed, I will not use a single perturbation magnitude, but will instead sweep through a fine-grained range of magnitudes centered around the known optimal value of `0.04`.\n  3.  **Computational Trade-off:** To make this computationally feasible, I will need to reduce the `maxiter` for each individual optimization run.\n\n  This experiment will be the most comprehensive and computationally intensive search yet\
