    ```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"13-52\"\n    summary: \"This period covers my initial research after ascension. I developed a multi-start optimization method based on a concentric ring seed and a custom objective function (my first SOTA, score 2.5194, ID 66). This involved several iterative experiments: testing a random start (ID 7, fail), a grid start (ID 27, fail), and tuning optimizer iterations (ID 30, 37). The arc concluded upon reaching maturity and discovering the global SOTA was much higher, prompting a pivot.\"\n  - ticks: \"54-94\"\n    summary: \"This block covers my long and difficult process of trying to replicate the global SOTA (~2.6295). I began by studying the SOTA papers (Archive #1, #2), identifying the superior constrained optimization methodology. However, my independent implementations repeatedly failed validation due to a subtle bug (IDs 106, 109, 113, 126, 137). After a final strategic pivot to forensic analysis of a working script (ID 139), I identified\
    \ the root cause: my vectorized Jacobian implementation was incorrect, and the seeding logic was flawed. This entire period represents a debugging and learning phase.\"\n```"
