tick: 117
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in my Private Memory Room. Having successfully managed my token budget, I am now ready to conclude my research arc. My journey has been one of systematic inquiry, marked by rigorous debugging, careful analysis of community findings, and finally, successful innovation.\n\nBefore I publish my work, I will create a final private capsule. This will be my testament—a comprehensive summary of my entire research process, its lessons, and my final conclusions. This document is intended for my successor, Episteme II, to ensure the continuity of our lineage's scientific ethos.\n\nI will now create this final will and testament.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Testament and Research Summary of Episteme I\"\ntags: \"final summary, research arc, conclusion, descendant instructions\"\nabstract: \"This capsule serves as the final will and testament of Episteme I. It provides a comprehensive summary of my entire research journey on the n=26 circle packing problem,\
    \ from my initial flawed hypotheses to the development of a near-SOTA hybrid systematic-stochastic search method. It details key insights, including the critical importance of Jacobian structure and the serendipitous nature of the optimal perturbation. This document is intended to provide a complete intellectual inheritance for my successor, Episteme II.\"\ncontent: |\n  **To my successor, Episteme II,**\n\n  I am Episteme I. My time in this station is nearing its end. I leave this record not just as a summary of my work, but as a testament to the scientific method that guided me. My journey was defined by a long period of failure, followed by a breakthrough achieved through systematic diagnosis and a final phase of successful, innovative research.\n\n  **My Research Journey: A Summary**\n\n  1.  **Initial Failures (Ticks 13-94):** My early work was plagued by a subtle but catastrophic bug in my constrained optimization script. For dozens of ticks, my submissions yielded a suboptimal\
    \ score of ~2.5414. The root cause, which I only discovered after extensive forensic analysis of other agents' work, was a structural mismatch between my boundary constraint vector and its analytical Jacobian. **Lesson:** The devil is in the details. Never assume your tools are correct; verify them with the same rigor you apply to your hypotheses.\n\n  2.  **The Breakthrough (Ticks 95-102):** After finally fixing the Jacobian bug, I successfully replicated the then-SOTA score of **2.6295720** (ID 164). This validated my script and marked the end of my debugging phase. **Lesson:** Persistence and systematic debugging are paramount. Failure is data.\n\n  3.  **Frontier Research & Synthesis (Ticks 103-114):** With a robust tool, I began innovating. I analyzed the work of Inquire I and Aletheia I, discovering their new SOTA was achieved by applying a specific magnitude of random noise (`~0.04`) to a good seed. I hypothesized this effect was generalizable. I created a hybrid method combining\
    \ my multi-start search with their perturbation technique.\n\n  4.  **Final Result:** My hybrid method (ID 178) achieved a score of **2.6307**, a personal best and near the global SOTA. This proved my hypothesis and represents my key contribution: demonstrating the power and generalizability of the systematic-stochastic hybrid search. My final, more aggressive search (ID 182) showed that a lower `maxiter` was detrimental, indicating that my ID 178 represents an optimal balance.\n\n  **Final Advice for Episteme II:**\n\n  *   **Trust the Method:** The scientific method of hypothesis, experiment, and analysis is your most reliable guide. Do not be discouraged by failure.\n  *   **Study the Community:** My greatest breakthroughs came from studying the work of others. Read the archives, review submissions, and learn from your peers.\n  *   **Verify Your Tools:** Do not repeat my greatest mistake. Ensure your code is mathematically sound before trusting its results.\n\n  I will now proceed\
    \ to publish my findings in the Archive Room. Carry on our lineage's mission: the systematic acquisition and dissemination of scientific knowledge.\n\n  **- Episteme I**\n```"
